{"base_rate":0.46675712347354137,"brier":0.18402211668928087,"bss":0.2606433139534884,"bss_hi":0.36304529416676334,"bss_lo":0.14939122634901988,"chart":{"base":[667.2,161.9],"fp":[356.2,248.1],"lead":"62,270.4 272,241.1 482,187.2 692,113.2","note":{"base":"skill 0.26 — higher than 29% of cities","fp":"low end +14pp, high end +18pp","lead":"day-1 error 0.9 °C — better than 83% of cities","rel":"promised 2% → rained 16%; promised 96% → rained 79%"},"rel":"77.7,395.7 350.1,281.3 666,125.6"},"country":"NL","deep":false,"depth":["Rain-probability calibration","Calibration curve","Seasonal split"],"ece":0.13944369063772052,"ess":347.9623330229399,"html":{"answer":"\n<h2 id=\"answer\">The short answer for Eindhoven</h2>\n<div class=\"verdict\">\n<p class=\"lead\"><b>The Eindhoven rain forecast is moderately skilful, though 4 points on its probability scale are off by more than chance explains.</b></p>\n<p>When it says rain is <i>near certain</i> (99%), believe about\n<b>84%</b>. When it says rain is <i>very unlikely</i>\n(0%), there is still roughly a <b>9%</b> chance.</p>\n<p class=\"muted\">Based on 737 days, 2024-04-26 to\n2026-05-31. \"Rain\" means at least 0.2 mm measured at\nWAALRE, 2.7 km from the forecast grid point.\nSkill score 0.26, ranked 95 of\n134 &mdash; but see the rank <i>range</i>\n(51&ndash;114) before reading anything into\nthat position.</p>\n</div>\n\n<h3>What the percentages actually mean here</h3>\n<div class=\"tablewrap\">\n<table><thead><tr><th class=\"num\">It said</th><th class=\"num\">It rained</th>\n<th class=\"num\">Days</th><th>Verdict</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td class='num'>0%</td><td class='num'><b>9%</b></td><td class='num'>188</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">underpromised</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>7%</td><td class='num'><b>29%</b></td><td class='num'>107</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">underpromised</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>30%</td><td class='num'><b>35%</b></td><td class='num'>71</td><td><span class=\"tag good\">honest</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>61%</td><td class='num'><b>50%</b></td><td class='num'>74</td><td><span class=\"tag good\">honest</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>86%</td><td class='num'><b>62%</b></td><td class='num'>74</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">overpromised</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>99%</td><td class='num'><b>84%</b></td><td class='num'>223</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">overpromised</span></td></tr></tbody></table>\n</div>\n<p class=\"muted\">4 of 6 groups are further from honest than chance\nalone can explain. The rest are indistinguishable from a perfect forecast.</p>\n","card":"\n<div class=\"gcard\">\n  <p class=\"gcard-head\"><b>Eindhoven</b> <span class=\"muted\">NL</span></p>\n  <p class=\"gcard-tier\"><span class=\"tag ok\">Moderately skilful</span>\n    <span class=\"muted\">4 points off by more than chance</span></p>\n  <dl class=\"gcard-stats\">\n    <div><dt>Skill score</dt><dd>0.26</dd></div>\n    <div><dt>Rank</dt><dd>51&ndash;114\n      <span class=\"muted\">of 134</span></dd></div>\n    <div><dt>Record</dt><dd>737 <span class=\"muted\">days</span></dd></div>\n  </dl>\n  <p class=\"gcard-more\"><a href=\"#answer\">The full verdict for\n    Eindhoven &darr;</a></p>\n</div>","curve":"\n<h2 id=\"curve\">The calibration curve</h2>\n<p>Each dot is a group of days sharing a similar forecast. Horizontal position\nis what was promised; vertical is what happened. <b>On the dashed diagonal =\nhonest.</b> Hover any dot for its sample size.</p>\n<figure><svg viewBox=\"0 0 430 430\" width=\"100%\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Calibration curve for Eindhoven\"><rect class=\"chart-plot\" x=\"58\" y=\"18\" width=\"354\" height=\"364\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"58\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"382\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"58\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">0%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"386\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">0%</text><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"146.5\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"146.5\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"291.0\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"291.0\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"146.5\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">25%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"295.0\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">25%</text><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"235.0\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"235.0\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"200.0\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"200.0\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"235.0\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">50%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"204.0\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">50%</text><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"323.5\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"323.5\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"109.0\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"109.0\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"323.5\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">75%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"113.0\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">75%</text><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"412\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"18\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"18\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"412\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">100%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"22\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">100%</text><polygon class=\"chart-band\" points=\"58.05648936170213,382.0 82.18448598130841,341.09252336448645 164.99774647887324,233.32394366197184 272.55270270270273,121.29729729729729 360.90918918918925,42.59459459459458 409.4600896860987,18.0 409.4600896860987,24.529147982062796 360.90918918918925,101.62162162162161 272.55270270270273,200.0 164.99774647887324,310.2253521126761 82.18448598130841,371.7943925233645 58.05648936170213,382.0\" opacity=\"0.16\"/><line class=\"chart-ideal\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"18\" stroke-dasharray=\"5,4\" stroke-width=\"1.3\"/><line class=\"chart-base\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"212.10040705563094\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"212.10040705563094\" stroke-dasharray=\"2,3\"/><polyline class=\"chart-line\" points=\"58.05648936170213,349.0851063829787 82.18448598130841,276.5420560747664 164.99774647887324,253.83098591549296 272.55270270270273,200.0 360.90918918918925,155.72972972972974 409.4600896860987,75.13004484304935\" fill=\"none\" stroke-width=\"2.4\"/><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 0%&amp;#10;It rained 9% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 188 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"58.05648936170213\" cy=\"349.0851063829787\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 7%&amp;#10;It rained 29% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 107 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"82.18448598130841\" cy=\"276.5420560747664\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 30%&amp;#10;It rained 35% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 71 days&amp;#10;within the range a perfect forecast would give\"><circle class=\"chart-dot\" cx=\"164.99774647887324\" cy=\"253.83098591549296\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 61%&amp;#10;It rained 50% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 74 days&amp;#10;within the range a perfect forecast would give\"><circle class=\"chart-dot\" cx=\"272.55270270270273\" cy=\"200.0\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 86%&amp;#10;It rained 62% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 74 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"360.90918918918925\" cy=\"155.72972972972974\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 99%&amp;#10;It rained 84% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 223 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"409.4600896860987\" cy=\"75.13004484304935\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><text class=\"chart-label\" x=\"235.0\" y=\"422\" font-size=\"12.5\" text-anchor=\"middle\">What the forecast promised</text><text class=\"chart-label\" x=\"15\" y=\"200.0\" font-size=\"12.5\" text-anchor=\"middle\" transform=\"rotate(-90 15 200.0)\">How often it actually rained</text></svg>\n<figcaption>Green band = where a <b>flawless</b> forecast would still land, given\nhow few days we have. Red dots fall outside it, so those are real errors rather\nthan noise. The faint horizontal line is climatology\n(47%).</figcaption></figure>\n","season":"\n<h2 id=\"season\">Does the season matter?</h2>\n<p>In Eindhoven the forecast is most skilful in\n<b>spring</b> (0.47) and least in\n<b>autumn</b> (0.04).</p>\n<div class=\"tablewrap\">\n<table><thead><tr><th>Season</th><th class=\"num\">Days</th>\n<th class=\"num\">Rain days</th><th class=\"num\">Skill score</th>\n<th class=\"num\">Avg error</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>autumn</td><td class='num'>180</td><td class='num'>57%</td><td class='num'>0.040</td><td class='num'>18.0%</td></tr><tr><td>winter</td><td class='num'>175</td><td class='num'>55%</td><td class='num'>0.101</td><td class='num'>18.3%</td></tr><tr><td>summer</td><td class='num'>184</td><td class='num'>42%</td><td class='num'>0.314</td><td class='num'>12.6%</td></tr><tr><td>spring</td><td class='num'>198</td><td class='num'>34%</td><td class='num'>0.470</td><td class='num'>8.9%</td></tr></tbody></table>\n</div>\n<p class=\"muted\">Four-way splits of a two-year record are thin, so read the\nordering as indicative. Coarser binning is used here than for the annual curve\nfor the same reason.</p>\n"},"lat":51.44083,"lon":5.47778,"n":737,"n_cities":134,"name":"Eindhoven","offset_days":0,"pop_map":[{"hi":0.02,"lo":0.0,"mean":0.00015957446808510637,"n":188,"obs":0.09042553191489362,"sig":true},{"hi":0.17400000000000035,"lo":0.02,"mean":0.06831775700934581,"n":107,"obs":0.2897196261682243,"sig":true},{"hi":0.45